==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|shake-down}}

===Etymology===
{{compound|shake|down|lang=en}}, from the phrase "[[shake down]]".

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|slang}} [[extortion|Extortion]], especially through [[blackmail]]
#: ''What is this, a '''shakedown'''?''
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[thorough]] [[search]]; a [[frisk]]
# A [[trial]] or [[test]] [[period]], especially of a [[ship]] or [[aircraft]]
# An improvised [[bed]].
#* '''1915''', [[w:W. Somerset Maugham|W.S. Maugham]], "[[s:Of Human Bondage/Chapter_CXIV|Of Human Bondage]]":
#*: "You'd better lie down for a bit. I expect you're about [[done up]]." -- "There's nowhere for me to lie down, sir," he answered, and there was in his voice a humbleness which was very distressing. -- "Don't you know anyone in the house who'll give you a '''shakedown'''?" -- "No, sir."

